---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro'
import AssertionCard from '../../components/AssertionCard.astro'
import ChartFigure from '../../components/ChartFigure.astro'
import Gloss from '../../components/Gloss.astro'
import { assertion } from '../../lib/feeds'
import { bar } from '../../lib/chart-spec'

const all = assertion('twelve-hundred-and-sixty-audits')
const routine = assertion('ninety-seven-per-cent-is-routine')
const companies = assertion('a-quarter-of-the-audited-are-private')
const counts = assertion('forty-five-governments-and-a-hundred-and-eighteen-bodies')
const overlap = assertion('the-lists-agree-where-they-overlap')

const sixty = assertion('sixty-two-findings-for-recovery')
const fivetimes = assertion('a-township-audit-is-five-times-as-likely')
const nine = assertion('nine-of-twelve-townships-and-seven-of-eight-villages')
const cities = assertion('the-county-and-both-cities-are-in-the-list')
const court = assertion('ninety-three-thousand-and-three-hundred-thousand')
const found = assertion('the-court-found-it-in-its-own-books')

const asked = assertion('fort-shawnee-asked-for-the-analysis')
const three = assertion('three-of-six-conditions-and-fifty-thousand-dollars')
const promised = assertion('more-promised-than-banked')
const ballot = assertion('twenty-five-months-to-the-ballot')
const lastday = assertion('the-last-day-of-record-is-june-2013')

const rateCats = ['Village', 'Township', 'Everything else', 'School district']
const rateVals = [14.7, 12.7, 2.5, 2.8]

const fundCats = ['Street Construction', 'General', 'Water Contract', 'State Reparations', 'Street Improvement Levy', 'Contract Police', 'Permissive Motor Vehicle']
const fundVals = [214273, 31692, 19948, 16616, -11636, -54657, -81468]

const rateSpec = bar(rateCats, rateVals, {
  yTitle: 'Audit reports carrying a finding for recovery, per cent',
  tickSuffix: '%',
  labelValues: true,
})

const fundSpec = bar(fundCats, fundVals, {
  yTitle: 'Fund balance, 31 May 2010, dollars',
  labelValues: true,
})
---

<Article slug="the-smallest-books">
  <p>
    Every public body in Ohio that handles public money is audited by the state, and the reports go
    into one search. Filtered to Allen County it returns twelve hundred and sixty of them, going
    back to 1999, on everything from the county itself to a cemetery association and a village that
    no longer exists. It is the only account here of how this county's governments keep their books
    rather than what they spend them on.
  </p>

  <h2>What the state audits here</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={all} open />
  <AssertionCard assertion={routine} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={companies} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={counts} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={overlap} />
  <Gloss>
    Two state counts of the same county's public bodies, forty-five and a hundred and eighteen, and
    neither is wrong. One counts units with a levy and a governing board in a single year. The other
    counts twenty-seven years of everything the state has had cause to audit, which includes private
    companies taking Medicaid money and a village its own electors abolished in 2012.
  </Gloss>

  <h2>Sixty-two findings</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={sixty} open />
  <AssertionCard assertion={fivetimes} />
  <ChartFigure
    id="classes"
    title="The rate runs with the size of the office, not the size of the budget"
    caption="Share of audit reports carrying a finding for recovery, by class of body, 1999 to 2026. A finding for recovery is an order that named money be repaid; the file does not carry the amount."
    columns={['Class', 'Reports with a finding, per cent']}
    rows={rateCats.map((c, i) => [c, rateVals[i]])}
    height={290}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="classes" set:html={JSON.stringify(rateSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={nine} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={cities} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={court} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={found} />

  <h2>A village that asked</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={asked} open />
  <AssertionCard assertion={three} />
  <ChartFigure
    id="funds"
    title="Three funds in the red and one holding more than the whole treasury"
    caption="The Village of Fort Shawnee's fund balances at 31 May 2010, as the Auditor of State found them. The village had no debt outstanding and had missed no payroll; its treasury held $164,982 against $315,419 promised to these funds."
    columns={['Fund', 'Balance']}
    rows={fundCats.map((c, i) => [c, fundVals[i]])}
    height={330}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="funds" set:html={JSON.stringify(fundSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={promised} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={ballot} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={lastday} />
</Article>
